.TH TM 1 "2026-11-07" "Topology Machine 1.0.0" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
tm \- discrete topology circuit workbench
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B tm
.I command
.RI [ options ]
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B tm
evaluates finite Boolean DAGs, GF(2^8) products, reversible gates,
two-to-four qubit amplitude circuits in an OpenQASM 3 subset, and
small dense nodal systems. It is a software workbench. It does not
claim a complexity-class separation, a quantum-hardware result, or a
physical energy bound.
.SH COMMANDS
.TP
.B help
Print usage and exit 0.
.TP
.B version
Print
.B tm 1.0.0
.
.TP
.B self-check \fR[\fB\-\-out-dir\fR \fIDIR\fR]
Run the native bundle and write QASM, SMT-LIB, and the GF netlist.
.TP
.B oracle
Print the decimal lines that
.I klong/oracle.kg
must match.
.TP
.B bench
Print one wall-clock sample per kernel.
.TP
.B dag eval \-\-expr \fIEXPR\fR \-\-input \fIN\fR
.TQ
.B dag truth \-\-expr \fIEXPR\fR \fR[\fB\-\-bits\fR \fIN\fR]
Expressions are
.BR 0 ,
.BR 1 ,
.BI i k\fR,
.BR not(e) ,
.BR and(e,e) ,
.BR or(e,e) ,
and
.BR xor(e,e) .
Input bit 0 is the least significant bit.
.TP
.B gf mul \fIA\fR \fIB\fR
.TQ
.B gf inv \fIA\fR
.TQ
.B gf pow \fIA\fR \fIEXP\fR
.TQ
.B gf check \fR[\fB\-\-full\fR]
.TQ
.B gf circuit \-\-out \fIFILE\fR
AES polynomial
.BR 0x11b .
.B \-\-full
checks all 16777216 associativity and distributivity triples.
.TP
.B rev apply \-\-width \fIN\fR \-\-state \fIS\fR \-\-prog \fIPROG\fR
.TQ
.B rev check
Gates are
.BR cx ,
.BR ccx ,
and
.BR cswap .
Wires are decimal and must be distinct.
.TP
.B qasm bell \-\-out \fIFILE\fR
.TQ
.B qasm reversible \-\-out \fIFILE\fR
.TQ
.B qasm sim \fIFILE\fR
The simulator accepts the subset this program emits, at most 4 qubits.
Measurement is not sampled.
.TP
.B analog solve \-\-g \fIROWS\fR \-\-i \fIVALUES\fR
Rows are separated by semicolons and entries by commas, in the C locale.
.TP
.B smt involution \-\-out \fIFILE\fR
.TQ
.B smt check
Writes or reads the fixed 3-bit involution query.
.B smt check
is an 8-state reading of that query. It prints
.B unsat
when no counterexample state exists. An external solver is optional.
.SH EXIT STATUS
.TP
.B 0
Success.
.TP
.B 1
A check that should hold failed.
.TP
.B 2
Usage or malformed input.
.TP
.B 3
Input/output error.
.TP
.B 4
Domain error, including a singular matrix, a missing field inverse, or an illegal wire.
.SH SEE ALSO
The project README, in particular the verification boundary.
